  "name": "@jahandco/mcp-server",
  "readme": "# Jah and Co Game SDK & CLI Model Context Protocol (MCP) Server\n\n[![npm version](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/@jahandco/mcp-server.svg)](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@jahandco/mcp-server)\n[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-blue.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)\n\nOfficial Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for autonomous AI coding agents (Claude Desktop, Cursor, Windsurf, Claude Code, Antigravity) to build, simulate, test, validate, and deploy titles on the **Jah and Co Platform** using `@jahandco/game-sdk`, `@jahandco/interactive-protocol`, `npx @jahandco/create`, and the `jc` CLI.\n\n---\n\n## Features\n\n- \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f **Project Scaffolding (`scaffold_title`)**: Bootstrap production-grade game titles with client scenes (`GameClient`), server rules isolate (`rules.ts`), and Webpack configuration for multiple genres (Turn-Based, Arcade, Card Battles, Rhythm).\n- \ud83d\udd0d **Deep Static AST & Isolate Validation (`validate_title`)**: Comprehensive checks for:\n  - Missing `engineReady` handling (prevents client loading screen hangs).\n  - Illegal browser DOM access (`window`, `document`) in server isolates.\n  - Illegal Node.js built-ins (`fs`, `child_process`) in session isolates.\n  - Strict Webpack single-bundle ES module rules build.\n  - Proper `Engine.launch()` and `GameClient` lifecycle hooks.\n- \u26a1 **In-Memory Rules Isolate Simulator (`simulate_rules_intent`)**: Execute and unit-test `handleIntent()` in memory with mock `BridgeEnvelope` and `WorkerContext` without requiring a browser or backend.\n- \ud83d\udcbb **CLI & Environment Tooling**: Check CLI installation, auto-install `jc`, manage developer projects, check auth credentials, start/stop local `jc dev` sandbox, and build/deploy to production.\n- \ud83d\udcda **Authoritative Resources (`gamesdk://docs/*`, `gamesdk://schemas/*`, `gamesdk://templates/*`)**: Instant, non-hallucinated access to SDK architecture guides, wire protocol JSON schemas, and code templates.\n- \ud83e\udd16 **Guided MCP Prompts**: Workflows for scaffolding new games, implementing multiplayer rules, isolate debugging, and production deployments.\n\n---\n\n## Quickstart\n\n### Running via npx (Zero Install)\n\n\\`\\`\\`bash\nnpx -y @jahandco/mcp-server@latest\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n### Running via JC CLI\n\n\\`\\`\\`bash\njc mcp\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n---\n\n## Client Configuration\n\n### Claude Desktop (`claude_desktop_config.json`)\n\nAdd the following to `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json` (macOS) or `%APPDATA%\\Claude\\claude_desktop_config.json` (Windows):\n\n\\`\\`\\`json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"jahandco-game-sdk\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@jahandco/mcp-server@latest\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n### Cursor / Windsurf / Antigravity (`mcp.json`)\n\n\\`\\`\\`json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"jahandco-game-sdk\": {\n      \"command\": \"jc\",\n      \"args\": [\"mcp\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n---\n\n## Tools Reference\n\n| Tool | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `scaffold_title` | Scaffold a game project (genres: `default`, `turn-based`, `card-game`, `rhythm`) |\n| `validate_title` | Run deep AST validation on manifest, isolate rules, client scenes, and webpack configs |\n| `simulate_rules_intent` | In-memory execution of `handleIntent()` with mock context and envelope |\n| `check_environment` | Inspect status of `jc` CLI, Node, pnpm, and Clerk auth session |\n| `install_jc_cli` | Automatically download and install `jc` binary to `~/.jahandco/bin` |\n| `whoami` | Check authenticated account and subscription tier |\n| `list_projects` | List Developer Platform projects |\n| `create_project` | Create a new platform project |\n| `link_project` | Link current directory to a platform project ID |\n| `start_dev_server` | Start local `jc dev` sandbox process |\n| `stop_dev_server` | Stop active `jc dev` sandbox process |\n| `get_dev_server_status` | View status and logs for running dev servers |\n| `build_and_deploy` | Validate, build client/rules bundles, and deploy to development/production |\n| `manage_assets` | List, upload, or remove game assets |\n\n---\n\n## Resources Reference\n\n- `gamesdk://docs/architecture`: Architecture overview & IoC pattern.\n- `gamesdk://docs/rules-engine`: Isolate execution contract, `handleIntent`, `reply`, `engineReady`.\n- `gamesdk://docs/game-client`: `GameClient` scene lifecycle & Phaser integration.\n- `gamesdk://docs/ui-kit`: Obsidian Slate tokens & HUD components.\n- `gamesdk://docs/wire-protocol`: `BridgeEnvelope` wire protocol specification.\n- `gamesdk://docs/jc-cli`: Full CLI command reference.\n- `gamesdk://schemas/{domain}`: JSON Schemas for `envelope`, `multiplayer`, `lobby`, `user`, `commerce`, `leaderboard`, `assets`.\n- `gamesdk://templates/{templateName}`: Production code templates.\n\n---\n\n## Development & Testing\n\n\\`\\`\\`bash\n# Build TypeScript\npnpm build\n\n# Run unit & integration test suite\npnpm test\n\n# Typecheck\npnpm typecheck\n\\`\\`\\`\n",
  "readmeFilename": "README.md",
